Given all the talk about anon FTP, this should prove interesting...

Last nite, I was FTPing around, looking for some AI (artificial intelligence)
code, as I am taking a class in it and wanted some code to analyze/run.
Anyway, I ftp'ed to a few sites I know of, downloaded some stuff.  Then I
checked ARCHIE for sites...found a few, went there, and looked around.
Then, being a good information locator, I thought of a few institutions that
do this type of research, but whose domain names I neither knew or got through
archie.  Therefore, I WHOIS'ed 'em, and found domain names for a few places
I hadn't looked yet.  (Stanford research Institute being one...SRI.COM).
Anyway, I browsed these, and ftp'ed to SRI.

  Well...they didnt have much.  I did a few GET foo.bar - just to display
the contents of some of the files on my screen.  One of them was named
passwrd.  (I didnt know what was in it).  I did a GET passwrd - and 
displayed its contents...apparently some binary or encrypted file having to 
do with (through powers of deduction and hindsight) their system passwords.
Like I knew?  Anyway, I didnt think mmuch of it (any of you sightread encrypted
textfiles?) and looked around a bit more, then left.  (I never downloaded
anything from them).

Point number 1:  I logged in as anonymous
point # 2: I sent them my full internet address for the password.

Now, g'wn figger....tonight, between classes, I jump on a terminal to check
my mail.  On my way out the door, I grab a phone and call home to check my
messages.  Theres a message on there from my prof saying "we need to talk.
Do _not_ log on to the vax again and try to break into SRI's computer system."

eh?

So I call him.  He says he got a call from the department chair, who got a
call from computer services, who got a call from an unknown person at SRI,
telling them someone at my university, having my name and email address
malisciously tried to break into their system last nite.  They say I tried to
log in using different usernames, and tried to take/change the passwords to
the system.

Pierce my ears and call me breezy!

Anyway, nmow I have to explain to: my prof, the dept. chair, the folks at
comp. srvcs., and quite possibly SRI (who, i am sure, will listen attentavely),
that I did nothing wrong.  I dont care if it was their ultra-secret hush-hush
higher-than-god password file.  I didnt know what it was, there was no 
indication of what it was, i couldnt decipher it, and it was in a public ftp 
site.  

Now then.  Where do they get off defaming my character and falsely accusing me?

anyway, if you cant guess, im still a bit steamed, but then again, I have
to take my GRE's in about 36 hours, and dont need this crap.  Opinions?
Suggestions?

